  "description": "Our lugged frame features a timeless aesthetic that can lean more retro or more modern, depending on how you design it.\n\nThe frame is hand-built from seamless, heat-treated, double-butted Reynolds 725 chromoly steel main tubes and forged track-style rear drops. There are braze-ons for two bottle cages on the down tube and seat tube. It also features beautiful hand-brazed lugged construction.\n\nThe fork features hand-brazed tapered chromoly steel with an investment-cast crown, 1-1/8\" steerer, and forged fork ends. It includes a Tange Seiki Technoglide headset with cartridge-type bearings. Choose your headset color from the dropdown menu.\n\nThe current colors are Oxide Red, a dark metallic red, and Heritage Blue, a medium metallic blue. There is limited stock of past colors, such as Iron Wine, a metallic plum; Sapphire Blue, a darker metallic blue; and Platinum White, a pearlized white. Custom colors are also an option. See more info here.\n\nTECH SPECS\n\nIncludes: Frame, fork, headset, and seatpost clamp.\n\nWeight: 5.9 lbs (55cm).\n\nAccepts 68mm English-standard bottom brackets.\n\nThreadless 1-1/8\" steerer tube.\n\n100mm front dropout spacing; 120mm rear dropout spacing.\n\n27.2mm seatpost compatible.\n\nAccommodates almost all track cranksets (tested to 135mm Q-factor).\n\nNote: No eyelets, braze-ons, or attachment points on the fork, dropouts, or seat/chain stays for fenders or racks.\n\nSIZING\n\nWe highly recommend reviewing our sizing page before purchasing. Look at both your height and your actual inseam/standover height. The guide below can also provide some general guidelines.\n\nRider Height\n\nFrame Size\n\nStandover Height\n\n5'4\" - 5'7\"\n\n49 CM\n\n30.2 IN\n\n5'7\" - 5'10\"\n\n52 CM\n\n31.3 IN\n\n5'10\" - 6'1\"\n\n55 CM\n\n32.5 IN\n\n6'1\" - 6'3\"\n\n58 CM\n\n33.6 IN\n\n6'3\" - 6'6\"\n\n60 CM\n\n34.8 IN\n\nFrame size is measured center-to-center of the seat tube. See more on our sizing page.\n\nCOMPONENT SIZING\n\nNote that our frames are designed around a 170mm crank arm length, a 24mm setback seatpost, and varying stem lengths based on frame size and rider height. You can find our stem length recommendations under the “Determining Bike Components Fit” section on the sizing page. If you choose different components, it may impact the fit.\n\nIMPORTANT NOTE ON COMPATIBILITY\n\nWe cannot guarantee the fit of any specific component set other than the ones we sell with our complete bikes. If you are planning a specific build, please contact us to see if we are aware of any issues. Even so, we will be unable to offer refunds based on lack of fit with any third-party components.",
